{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"The first broker-supervision change exposed the CI cause: Mosquitto exits with Unable to write pid file for /tmp/gnostic-mosquitto.pid, so neither readiness probe nor runner could connect.","decision":"Generate a minimal smoke-only Mosquitto config per invocation, place its pid file inside the invocation-owned temporary directory, run the process in the foreground, and retain the startup log until cleanup.","impact":"Changed only Scripts/container-smoke.sh and Scripts/runner-smoke.sh. The broker listener remains loopback-only and anonymous on the smoke port. No dependency or application behavior changed.","recurrence_control":"The smoke scripts capture broker startup errors, wait for a successful publish before testing consumers, and remove the temporary directory after stopping the child. bash -n, make harness-test, and git diff --check pass.","rejected_alternatives":["Keep the shared /tmp pid path, which fails in the CI container permissions context.","Wait longer on the same daemonized process after it has exited."],"sources":[]}
